{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":100436,"duration_api_ms":113761,"num_turns":4,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0e7a3f73-a55e-4b4a-bb9a-dc83221881c7","total_cost_usd":0.39090175,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29260,"cache_read_input_tokens":82247,"output_tokens":3584,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29260,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3798,"outputTokens":5427,"cacheReadInputTokens":39540,"cacheCreationInputTokens":33917,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.07728325,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3584,"cacheReadInputTokens":82247,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29260,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.31361849999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All seven amendments are valid and should be accepted. Amendments 1-3 address real constant/logic duplication between substrate.rs and microfauna.rs that risks silent divergence. Amendment 4 identifies a modeling simplification that should at minimum be documented. Amendments 5-7 identify genuine correctness bugs in the new per-stage molt system: the mineral floor is too permissive, mixed-stage outcomes corrupt shared state (net -0.05 penalty on mixed days instead of increased pressure), and the migration seeding path misidentifies fresh populations as legacy saves.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-0142f03c","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: substrate.rs:8 defines MICROFAUNA_O2_PER_MG_C_RESPIRED = 2.67, and microfauna.rs:7 defines O2_PER_MG_C_RESPIRED = 2.67. Same stoichiometric constant duplicated under two names. If either is updated independently, the substrate O2 demand estimate silently diverges from actual microfauna respiration. Extracting to a shared constant is straightforward and prevents this class of bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-0571fa0c","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the 0.01 magic number appears at substrate.rs:189 and microfauna.rs:73, both representing the daily detritus consumption fraction. The substrate module uses this to estimate O2 demand from microfauna activity, so it must stay synchronized with the actual consumption rate in microfauna.rs. A named constant eliminates the coupling risk."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-6ea35aba","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: substrate.rs:164-169 has an inline match with the same accessibility values as microfauna_periphyton_accessibility in microfauna.rs:157-164. There's actually already a subtle inconsistency — microfauna.rs applies .clamp(0.0, 1.0) to substrate_surface_access while substrate.rs does not. Sharing the function eliminates this existing drift and prevents future divergence."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-54222a0f","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: effective_substrate_porosity (substrate.rs:133-140) finds the first layer with depth > epsilon and uses only its porosity. When O2 penetration extends into deeper layers with different porosity, this single-layer approximation can materially skew the Bouldin diffusion calculation. At minimum, a documenting comment is warranted; ideally, a layered calculation."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-9ceac44a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified the math: with GH/Ca/Mg near zero, all three sub-factors floor at 0.3 (substrate.rs:1175-1176 clamp(0.3, 1.0)), yielding mineral_factor = 0.3*0.5 + 0.3*0.25 + 0.3*0.25 = 0.3. With condition=0.8 and stable environment: base_score = 0.45*0.3 + 0.35*0.8 + 0.10*1.0 + 0.10*1.0 = 0.615. condition_gate = min(0.8*3.0, 1.0) = 1.0, so success_score = 0.615. This passes any reasonable threshold (~0.55), defeating the severe-deficiency molt gate the patch intended to implement."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-37123d6e","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: lines 498-509 show that on a mixed-stage day (any_failed=true AND any_succeeded=true), failed_molt_accum gets +0.3 then -0.35, netting -0.05 — a mixed outcome actually *reduces* penalty. Additionally, last_molt_success is set to false by any failure and the !any_failed guard prevents success from restoring it, meaning a juvenile failure blocks sub-adult maturation (line 852) even when sub-adults succeeded. Both are clear correctness defects in shared state management."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7560ca22","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: StageCohort::default() sets molt_timer_days = 0.0 (biology.rs:112), while AnimalState::default() sets inter_molt_timer_days = 14.0 (biology.rs:615). The migration check (shrimp.rs:411-414) triggers whenever inter_molt_timer_days > 0 and all stage timers are 0. This condition is satisfied by freshly constructed populations, not just legacy saves. Result: juvenile stage (14-day interval) starts immediately molt-ready on day 1, and sub-adults start 2/3 through their cycle, producing spurious early molts and failures."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"dfd88cad-38d8-4a1a-b3f0-a1e895544162"}
